 the table.","Before the entrées arrive."],"correct":2,"explanation":""}},{"id":"createGuestServiceQuiz-5","source":"Guest Service Scenarios · August 21, 2026","review":false,"question":{"prompt":"What is the correct way to suggest dessert?","category":"Guest service","options":["Ask “Any dessert?” while walking away.","Bring the dessert menu back to the table and recommend one or two specific desserts.","Drop the check immediately and wait to see if they ask.","Tell guests dessert is available only if they are still hungry."],"correct":1,"explanation":""}},{"id":"createGuestServiceQuiz-6","source":"Guest Service Scenarios · August 21, 2026","review":false,"question":{"prompt":"When should the guest receive a printed copy of the check?","category":"Guest service","options":["Only if the guest asks to see one.","Only after payment has been completed.","Before payment is completed, so the guest can review the bill and see the included 18% gratuity before authorizing payment.","At the same time the receipt is thrown away."],"correct":2,"explanation":""}},{"id":"createGuestServiceQuiz-7","source":"Guest Service Scenarios · August 21, 2026","review":false,"question":{"prompt":"Why is the printed check presented before payment?","category":"Guest service","options":["So the guest has the opportunity to review charges and clearly see that 18% gratuity is already included before completing the transaction.","So the server can avoid discussing gratuity.","Only because some guests do not use credit cards.","Because the printed check replaces the need for payment."],"correct":0,"explanation":""}},{"id":"createGuestServiceQuiz-8","source":"Guest Service Scenarios · August 21, 2026","review":false,"question":{"prompt":"A guest reaches for the payment device before reviewing the printed check. What should the server do?","category":"Guest service","options":["Hide the gratuity line so the transaction is faster.","Complete payment as quickly as possible.","Politely present the printed check first and give the guest an opportunity to review it before completing payment.","Tell the guest they can review the bill after payment."],"correct":2,"explanation":""}},{"id":"createGuestServiceQuiz-9","source":"Guest Service Scenarios · August 21, 2026","review":false,"question":{"prompt":"A guest says, “I didn't realize gratuity was already included,” after seeing the printed check. What is the best response?","category":"Guest service","options":["Explain calmly that 18% gratuity is included on all checks and allow the guest to review the bill before payment.","Tell them it cannot be discussed.","Rush the transaction before they ask more questions.","Immediately remove the gratuity."],"correct":0,"explanation":""}},{"id":"createGuestServiceQuiz-10","source":"Guest Service Scenarios · August 21, 2026","review":false,"question":{"prompt":"A guest calls and wants to place a pickup order in advance. What is the correct response?","category":"Guest service","options":["Transfer the call to the kitchen.","Take the order over the phone and collect payment when they arrive.","Direct the guest to Uber Eats to pre-order for pickup; they may also come in and place the order in person.","Tell the guest JusTini's does not offer pickup."],"correct":2,"explanation":""}},{"id":"createGuestServiceQuiz-11","source":"Guest Service Scenarios · August 21, 2026","review":false,"question":{"prompt":"A guest calls for delivery. What should the employee do?","category":"Guest service","options":["Tell them to call back after closing.","Have them text the order to the restaurant.","Direct the guest to Uber Eats for delivery.","Take the order manually and find someone to deliver it."],"correct":2,"explanation":""}},{"id":"createGuestServiceQuiz-12","source":"Guest Service Scenarios · August 21, 2026","review":false,"question":{"prompt":"A guest refuses to use Uber Eats but still wants a phone order. What is the best response?","category":"Guest service","options":["Make an exception.","Take the order but do not send it to the kitchen.","Politely explain that pre-orders must go through Uber Eats, but the guest is welcome to come in and place the order in person.","Hang up."],"correct":2,"explanation":""}},{"id":"createGuestServiceQuiz-13","source":"Guest Service Scenarios · August 21, 2026","review":true,"question":{"prompt":"A guest arrives before the rest of their party and becomes upset that the party cannot be seated yet. What is the best response?","category":"Guest service","options":["Cancel the reservation.","Acknowledge the frustration, explain the full-party seating policy calmly, and offer a place to wait if available.","Say, “That's the rule,” and end the conversation.","Seat the incomplete party to avoid a complaint."],"correct":1,"explanation":""}},{"id":"createGuestServiceQuiz-14","source":"Guest Service Scenarios · August 21, 2026","review":true,"question":{"prompt":"The guest continues arguing after the full-party seating policy has been explained. What should the host do?","category":"Guest service","options":["Seat them anyway.","Ignore them completely.","Argue back.","Involve a manager rather than escalating the disagreement."],"correct":3,"explanation":""}},{"id":"createGuestServiceQuiz-15","source":"Guest Service Scenarios · August 21, 2026","review":true,"question":{"prompt":"A guest says, “I just don't like this dish.” What should the server do FIRST?","category":"Guest service","options":["Tell the guest they ordered it, so nothing can be done.","Immediately remove the item from the check.","Ask questions to find out what the guest does not like and determine whether there is an actual quality or preparation issue.","Take the plate away immediately."],"correct":2,"explanation":""}},{"id":"createGuestServiceQuiz-16","source":"Guest Service Scenarios · August 21, 2026","review":true,"question":{"prompt":"After speaking with the guest, the server determines there is NO quality or preparation issue; the guest simply does not prefer the item. What should the server explain?","category":"Guest service","options":["The guest must finish the item.","JusTini's does not remove items from the check based simply on personal preference, but the guest is welcome to order something else.","The item will automatically be comped.","The kitchen will remake the same item."],"correct":1,"explanation":""}},{"id":"createGuestServiceQuiz-17","source":"Guest Service Scenarios · August 21, 2026","review":true,"question":{"prompt":"A guest simply dislikes an item but wants to order a different entrée. What is the correct approach?","category":"Guest service","options":["Refuse to let them order anything else.","Tell them they must take the original dish home before ordering again.","Let them know they may order something else, while explaining that the original properly prepared item is not automatically removed based on preference.","Automatically comp both dishes."],"correct":2,"explanation":""}},{"id":"createGuestServiceQuiz-19","source":"Guest Service Scenarios · August 21, 2026","review":true,"question":{"prompt":"Why should the server avoid removing the food before the manager arrives when there is a complaint?","category":"Guest service","options":["The guest is required to keep all food on the table until closing.","The manager may need to see the item and understand exactly what the guest is reporting before deciding on the resolution.","Servers are never allowed to touch guest plates.","It guarantees the item will be comped."],"correct":1,"explanation":""}},{"id":"createGuestServiceQuiz-20","source":"Guest Service Scenarios · August 21, 2026","review":true,"question":{"prompt":"Which statement should a server NOT make before a manager has reviewed a quality issue?","category":"Guest service","options":["“I'll have my manager come over right away.”","“I'll definitely take this off your bill.”","“Can you tell me exactly what seems wrong with it?”","“Let me get my manager so we can take a look 